00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:16.620
THE STATE OF NVIDIA:
Nvidia is going to be the world’s largest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:23.220
company. For years, haters have been saying that&nbsp;
Nvidia’s time at the top is almost over. As soon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:29.280
as the custom PC hype dies down, Nvidia will get&nbsp;
crushed. As soon as the Bitcoin mining craze ends,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:35.280
Nvidia will be crushed. As soon as the supply&nbsp;
chain nightmare ends, Nvidia will be crushed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:42.240
But, time and time again, Nvidia has shown more&nbsp;
resilience than any big tech stock on the market.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:49.380
For example, just last year, Nvidia saw a 68% sell&nbsp;
off due to the recession and general fears about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:58.560
tech. But, unlike Intel who stayed down, Nvidia&nbsp;
has already rebounded a 158%. In fact, they’re&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:04.680
only 20% away from their all time highs as we&nbsp;
speak. This makes Nvidia the 7th largest company&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:11.580
in the world with a market cap of $650 billion.&nbsp;
But, that’s not to say that the haters don’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:18.480
have some valid concerns like Nvidia’s valuation.&nbsp;
Nvidia is hands down the most richly valued big&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:24.420
tech company, even more richly valued than Tesla.&nbsp;
Take their financials for example. In the past 12&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:31.020
months, Nvidia has only pulled in $4.3 billion&nbsp;
in net income. For perspective, if Apple was the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:38.640
same size as Nvidia, they would be pulling in $25&nbsp;
billion or over 5 times more. But, just because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:44.100
Nvidia has a rich valuation doesn’t mean that they&nbsp;
wont continue growing in terms of fundamentals and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:50.100
market cap. In fact, it’s highly likely that this&nbsp;
is the case. They’ve got a foot in consumer grade&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:57.720
products, a foot in enterprise grade products, and&nbsp;
a ginormous foot in AI. But, it wasn’t always like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.720 --> 00:02:05.760
this. Nvidia has been around since 1993, and up&nbsp;
until 2016, this is how their stock graph looked.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:12.060
So, here’s how Nvida went from being a no name&nbsp;
background company to becoming the world’s largest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:17.880
semi conductor company all within a matter of 7&nbsp;
years and why all of this is just the beginning.

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:20.560
BITCOIN BANANZA:&nbsp;

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:28.200
Taking a look back, Nvidia’s exponential run can&nbsp;
be traced back to early to mid 2016. At the time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:34.440
Nvidia primarily served a niche market of gamers.&nbsp;
They had a decent presence in enterprise. Their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:39.660
most notable enterprise client was likely Tesla.&nbsp;
If you didn’t know, it was Nvidia’s GPUs that were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:45.240
initially powering Tesla’s autonomous features.&nbsp;
But, Tesla itself wasn’t exactly a big company.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:50.760
In fact, they were simply fighting for their own&nbsp;
survival and they were actually most shorted stock&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:57.840
of all time. So, really, Nvidia’s main business&nbsp;
was selling gpus to gamers, but all of this would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:03.720
change with Bitcoin’s bull run. You might be&nbsp;
asking what does Bitcoin have to do with GPUs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:09.840
well the answer is actually everything. The way&nbsp;
that Bitcoins become available on the market is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:15.180
through a computationally intense process&nbsp;
called mining. And it turns out that Nvidia&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:19.920
GPUs are often the most cost effective way to&nbsp;
mine various crypto currencies. Since then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:24.720
many of the top cryptos have actually become&nbsp;
too computationally intense for Nvidia GPUs to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:29.640
handle or they’ve switched to a proof of stake&nbsp;
model which eliminates the need for GPUs. But,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:35.700
despite this, the vast majority of the most&nbsp;
profitable GPUs are still from Nvidia. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:41.400
you can imagine how lucrative this was back in the&nbsp;
day. Miners would go out and buy dozens, hundreds,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:48.180
thousands of GPUs each. As you would imagine, this&nbsp;
led to an extraordinary amount of demand and it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:53.700
wasn’t long until Nvidia’s supply started running&nbsp;
out, leading to GPU prices skyrocketing. Nvidia&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:59.940
GPUs were regularly selling for 50 to 100% more on&nbsp;
secondary markets and Nvidia actually got a bunch&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.940 --> 00:04:05.220
of flak from the gaming community. Many of them&nbsp;
felt that Nvidia was selling into this fad instead&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:09.900
of supporting their main demographic. They felt&nbsp;
that Nvidia should be implementing quantity limits&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:15.240
and nerfing the mining power of their cards to&nbsp;
ensure that gamers could still get GPUs for MSRP,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.240 --> 00:04:21.540
but this didn’t exactly happen. Nvidia very much&nbsp;
played into the mining craze and let the miners&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.540 --> 00:04:28.200
establish a new normal price for GPUs. This led&nbsp;
to a mini movement against Nvidia where a bunch&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:32.820
of gamers switched to AMD. AMD was crushing&nbsp;
it against Intel with their Ryzen series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.820 --> 00:04:36.660
so many gamers were hopeful that they&nbsp;
would also be able to take on Nvidia,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:42.240
but this never really materialized. While AMD&nbsp;
has been able to hold their own against Nvidia,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:48.660
Nvidia is still very much the GPU king. But, it&nbsp;
wasn’t all good news for Nvidia back in 2018.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.660 --> 00:04:55.560
Bitcoin’s price would peak out at the end of 2017&nbsp;
and it would dramatically crash 83% right after.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.560 --> 00:05:00.960
This took out much of the appeal of crypto mining&nbsp;
and it didn’t take long for miners to leave the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:06.360
scene. For gamers, this was Nvidia’s judgement&nbsp;
day. They had to pay the price for siding with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.360 --> 00:05:12.960
miners instead of gamers. And I guess they did&nbsp;
pay some price. Once the mining craze died down,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.960 --> 00:05:20.100
Nvidia’s stock would drop 57%. But, with that&nbsp;
being said, the mining boom allowed Nvidia to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.100 --> 00:05:27.660
grow 11X in the prior 18 months, so I don’t&nbsp;
think they were exactly sad. If anything they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:32.280
were optimistic as they were determined to make&nbsp;
the price increases due to mining permanent.

00:05:32.280 --> 00:05:37.380
THE PRICES STICK:
Everyone was expecting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.380 --> 00:05:44.880
for GPU prices to plummet as soon the miners left,&nbsp;
but Nvidia had a different idea. You see, just as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:50.760
the mining craze was dying down, Nvidia would come&nbsp;
out with the 2000 series of GPUs. Let’s just say,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.760 --> 00:05:56.640
it was substantially more expensive especially&nbsp;
when it came to the high end cards. The GTX 1080&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.640 --> 00:06:04.440
for example launched for $600. The RTX 2080 though&nbsp;
came in at $700 to $800. The real difference was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.440 --> 00:06:12.180
in the TI series though. The GTX 1080 ti launched&nbsp;
for $700. The RTX 2080 ti, however, came in at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:19.440
$1000 to $1100 or 50% more. Nvidia’s justification&nbsp;
for these price increases were that they added&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:25.740
ray tracing technology which is a notable upgrade,&nbsp;
but it didn’t exactly warrant a price hike and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.740 --> 00:06:32.640
proof can be seen in Nvidia’s financials. Between&nbsp;
2016 and 2018, Nvidia’s net margin would nearly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.640 --> 00:06:40.654
triple from just 13% to 37%. Clearly, the cost&nbsp;
difference to add RTX was nowhere near as large&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.654 --> 00:06:45.780
as the price jumps, but gamers were still hopeful.&nbsp;
They were optimistic that Nvidia would realize&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.780 --> 00:06:50.100
that these prices were unaffordable for most&nbsp;
gamers and that they would eventually decrease&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.100 --> 00:06:57.120
prices. But, Nvidia would stubbornly hold on and&nbsp;
gamers would eventually compromise. The ones that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.120 --> 00:07:01.860
didn’t would end up having to pay even more&nbsp;
as Nvidia would experience yet another boom in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.860 --> 00:07:07.980
2020. As everyone knows, 2020 brought with it the&nbsp;
pandemic which caused everyone to stay at home.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.980 --> 00:07:13.320
This led to an unprecedented number of people&nbsp;
buying gaming PCs and getting into gaming. But,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.320 --> 00:07:19.620
the pandemic didn’t just bring more demand, it&nbsp;
also brought less supply. When China is shut down&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:23.820
every other week and there are new obstacles&nbsp;
in every step of the production process from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.820 --> 00:07:29.280
factories to logistics, it’s no wonder why&nbsp;
companies entered a supply chain crises. For&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.280 --> 00:07:34.680
companies that relied on volume of goods sold,&nbsp;
this was devastating. But, for a company like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:40.800
Nvidia who could just jack up the prices, this&nbsp;
was a gold rush, and don’t even get me started on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.800 --> 00:07:46.440
the secondary markets. Remember how prices were&nbsp;
hiked 50 to 100% during the mining boom. Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:54.060
this time prices would be hiked 3, 5 10X. People&nbsp;
were literally auctioning off GPUs as if it was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.060 --> 00:07:59.160
some sort of antique product and Nvidia would of&nbsp;
course just fuel the fire with yet another series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.160 --> 00:08:05.400
of cards: the 3000 series. This time Nvidia took&nbsp;
the Apple approach. They realized that they get a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.400 --> 00:08:11.220
bunch of backlash when they increase the price of&nbsp;
a given series. So, they decided, why not just add&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:11.220 --> 00:08:18.420
another tier of GPUs like the iPhone Pro series.&nbsp;
And with that we saw the launch of the RTX 3090&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.420 --> 00:08:26.580
for $1500 and the RTX 3090 TI for $2000. But, it&nbsp;
didn’t stop right there either. If you’re familiar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.580 --> 00:08:32.640
with Bitcoin, you know that it usually follows&nbsp;
a 4 year cycle, and it had already been 4 years&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.640 --> 00:08:39.720
since 2016. Yes, the miners were back and this&nbsp;
time Nvidia was ready for them. In early 2021,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.720 --> 00:08:45.420
Nvidia would go ahead and nerf gaming GPUs with&nbsp;
software so that they couldn’t be used for mining.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:51.720
Instead, they would go ahead and launch mining&nbsp;
specific GPUs that cost um $4700. Originally,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.720 --> 00:08:56.100
gamers were hoping that such a move would be&nbsp;
beneficial for them. But now, they were paying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.100 --> 00:09:01.500
a ludicrous amount and miners were paying an even&nbsp;
more ludicrous amount. If you thought gamers and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.500 --> 00:09:05.760
miners were lucrative though, just wait till&nbsp;
you hear what gold mine they tripped on next.

00:09:05.760 --> 00:09:09.300
AI BOOM:&nbsp;

00:09:09.300 --> 00:09:14.340
It turns out that GPUs aren’t just capable&nbsp;
of making your games look better. They’re&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.340 --> 00:09:20.700
also a requirement for machine learning and AI&nbsp;
training. I’m sure you know about ChatGPT by now.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:28.380
ChatGPT was trained using a bunch of Nvidia GPUs&nbsp;
called the H100. The H100 runs between $10 and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:34.500
$20,000 depending on what specs you get, we can&nbsp;
call it $15,000 on average. This is obviously an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.500 --> 00:09:39.660
unreasonable amount for you an me, but surely&nbsp;
that’s nothing for a company right? Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.660 --> 00:09:45.600
that would be the case until you realize that&nbsp;
ChatGPT needed 10,000 of these suckers just for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:50.820
the initial training. If you haven’t done the&nbsp;
math yet, that’s $150 million. Even accounting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.820 --> 00:09:55.740
for a discount due to the scale, we’re talking&nbsp;
about $100 million and that was just for phase&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.740 --> 00:10:01.860
one of development for 1 project. Given&nbsp;
the success of ChatGPT, you can bet that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.860 --> 00:10:06.360
every tech company and their mothers want a&nbsp;
piece of the pie. The most notable example is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:06.360 --> 00:10:11.400
probably Google Bard. Over the past couple of&nbsp;
years, Google has tried to develop their own&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:11.400 --> 00:10:17.640
computational devices called TPUs, but Google has&nbsp;
by no means been able to replace Nvidia. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:17.640 --> 00:10:21.660
I don’t even think they’re trying to replace&nbsp;
Nvidia as they’re actually promoting Nvidia&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:21.660 --> 00:10:27.480
products. They’re literally cloudifying Nvidia&nbsp;
GPUs and making that into it’s own business. If&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.480 --> 00:10:31.920
buying this much computation power for your&nbsp;
AI business is bit too much, don’t worry,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:31.920 --> 00:10:37.620
you can just rent it from Google instead. Most&nbsp;
tech giants, however, are opting to just work with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:37.620 --> 00:10:43.860
Nvidia directly though. Tesla for example is using&nbsp;
5760 Nvidia A100 GPUs to train their self driving.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:43.860 --> 00:10:50.340
Each of these GPUs costs a cool 10 Gs, so Tesla’s&nbsp;
setup costs $57 million not including the setup,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:50.340 --> 00:10:55.860
maintenance, and lease. A similar story can be&nbsp;
seen with Meta as well. They’ve actually been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:55.860 --> 00:11:04.440
using Nvidia GPUs since 2017 when got access to&nbsp;
22,000 of their V100 GPUs. As you can see, Nvidia&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:04.440 --> 00:11:11.400
is not just a monopoly in this sector, they’re&nbsp;
literally the only viable solution. And that’s not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:11.400 --> 00:11:18.780
because of a lack of competition. Companies like&nbsp;
AMD, Intel, Qualcomm, TSMC, and AWS all see this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:18.780 --> 00:11:24.120
opportunity. It’s just extraordinarily difficult&nbsp;
to catch up to Nvidia when they have a lead of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:24.120 --> 00:11:30.480
20 to 30 years in the GPU scene. So, let’s just&nbsp;
say, Nvidia ain’t going anywhere anytime soon.

00:11:30.480 --> 00:11:31.860
THE FUTURE OF NVIDIA:
Hearing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:34.080 --> 00:11:40.560
all this, you might be saying that Nvidia just got&nbsp;
lucky with all these booms. They just got lucky&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:40.560 --> 00:11:45.000
that there was a gaming boom and then a mining&nbsp;
boom and then a machine learning boom and then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:51.660
an AI boom, but that’s completely untrue. Luck is&nbsp;
what happens when preparation meets opportunity.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:51.660 --> 00:11:58.620
The reality is that Nvidia saw this vision 30&nbsp;
years ago in 1993. It simply wasn’t till 23&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:58.620 --> 00:12:04.080
years later that the rest of the world realized&nbsp;
how vital this technology really was. First, it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:04.080 --> 00:12:08.640
was the gaming community, then it was the mining&nbsp;
community, then it was the enterprise community,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:08.640 --> 00:12:15.120
and now it’s the AI community, but they’re by&nbsp;
no means the last to realize the potential of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:15.120 --> 00:12:20.100
GPUs. While it’s unfortunate that it took so&nbsp;
long for everyone else to get on the same page,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:20.100 --> 00:12:25.800
it gave Nvidia an extraordinary amount of time&nbsp;
to cement themselves as the undisputed king.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:25.800 --> 00:12:30.540
And unlike Intel who blundered their lead&nbsp;
by stagnating, Nvidia is still innovating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:30.540 --> 00:12:36.480
as fast as ever which has made it impossible&nbsp;
for anyone else to outdo them. Now of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:36.480 --> 00:12:41.700
all companies will eventually become like&nbsp;
Intel, but that’s not happening to Nvidia&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:41.700 --> 00:12:47.640
in the imminent future. Here’s what’s happening&nbsp;
instead. Tech itself is a gold mine and you have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:47.640 --> 00:12:53.220
all these companies Google, Microsoft, Tesla,&nbsp;
Apple, Facebook all digging for gold. So far,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:53.220 --> 00:12:58.380
they’ve been pretty successful at finding gold,&nbsp;
but whether they hit gold or not doesn’t matter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:58.380 --> 00:13:02.820
for Nvidia because they’re the ones selling&nbsp;
the shovels and that’s why Nvidia will become&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:02.820 --> 00:13:07.860
the world’s largest company. The only company&nbsp;
that can steal this title from Nvidia in my&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:07.860 --> 00:13:14.400
opinion is Tesla. Do you agree? Comment that down&nbsp;
below. Also, drop a like if you would like to see&nbsp;&nbsp;

